// Title: File Download Via InstallUtil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 75edd216-1939-4c73-8d61-7f3a0d85b5cc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects use of .NET InstallUtil.exe in order to download arbitrary files. The files will be
//   written to "%LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\INetCache\IE\"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/pull/239
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_installutil_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\InstallUtil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "InstallUtil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
